    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0586" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg546"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1541.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your despatch of the 10th
                    ultimo, No. 1031, and to my Nos. 1525 and 1539, I transmit a copy of a letter of
                    the 16th ultimo, from Messrs. J. O. Merrill &amp; Co., of San Francisco, part
                    owners and agents of the whaling bark William G. Nye relative to the claim
                    against the British government, on behalf of the owners of that vessel, to
                    indemnity for losses growing out of her destruction by the Shenandoah or Sea
                    King.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., London.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d332-a1.xml" xpointer="d332-a1"/>
            </div>
